---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DrealNote from '@/components/DrealNote.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who runs this site and how to reach him.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I am a site reliability engineer. Before that I was a network engineer, with a bias towards security and
      automation that never went away. I like systems that fail loudly, documentation that tells the truth, and
      tools that work offline.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. If it matters, encrypt it: the key is on the
      <a href="/pgp">PGP page</a> and discoverable via WKD, so <code>gpg --locate-keys {SITE.email}</code> just works.
    </p>
    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      Static, no tracking, no third-party requests. How it is built is documented in
      <a href="/projects/site-platform">the platform notes</a>; the source, including every architecture decision,
      is on <a href="https://github.com/ivanpanev/ivanpanev.net">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Zen Old Mincho for headings, Zen Kaku Gothic New for body, JetBrains Mono for code, all self-hosted.
      Three accents — koke, murasaki, kaki — on one washi canvas, picked randomly the first time you
      visit and remembered afterwards; change them from the toggle in the header.
    </p>
  </article>
  <DrealNote />
</BaseLayout>
